 ———————— FORBIDDEN Chaos By Design US Tour 2026 Godfathers
  in the Bay Area metal scene\, Forbidden have returned with their first al
 bum in 16 years to unleash 12 fierce\, uncompromising\, and supremely prog
 ressive songs which signal an almighty return. Forbidden will be released 
 by BLKIIBLK Records and charts a defiant journey through scything riffs\, 
 incredible melodies\, 24 karat lead guitars\, simply thunderous drums and 
 bass\, plus the studio debut of Norman Skinner (Niviane & Imagika) whose s
 oaring vocals elevate the material to unprecedented levels. Conceived by f
 ounder and guitarist Craig Locicero alongside his creative brother\, drumm
 er Chris Kontos\, the foundational energy of bassist Matt Camacho\, the ve
 rsatility and poise of guitarist Jeremy Von Epp\, and Skinner’s voraciou
 s fresh approach\, Forbidden sees the band arriving at their finest hour w
 ith their richest-ever line-up. With Skinner stepping up to take on lyrica
 l duties\, Forbidden takes a fierce and uncompromising look into the eyes 
 of our times without taking sides\, instead imploring people to recognize 
 the false conflicts created by the current society and how they can conque
 r and rise above them. Take the blistering roar of “Single Point Failure
 ”\, the beautiful orchestral savagery of “Flower of Life”\, and the 
 relentless charge of “Burning The Lungs Of Earth.” There’s also the 
 mid-paced brooding power of “Psyclops\,” the twisting\, winding power 
 force of “Sycophantasy” featuring guest vocals from Mastodon’s Brann
  Dailor\, and a thunderous ode to women “The Burden” featuring guest v
 ocals from Kayla Dixon. In addition\, Forbidden pay homage to classic Amer
 ican heavy metal band\, Savatage in the shape of a malevolent and mesmeric
  cover of “Sirens”\, which embraces Greek mythology. Recorded\, produc
 ed and engineered at Sharkbite Studios in Oakland\, California with engine
 er and co-producer Zack Ohren\, Forbidden is the the resounding realizatio
 n of a band which has finally found inner-peace\, and furious cohesion\, i
 n expressing its true passionate angst and incredible metal heart. Check o
 ut Forbidden here! Website | Instagram | Facebook Supported By: Heathen\, 
